Matt Welch here with my co-author Nick  Gillespie of the Declaration of  Independence how libertarian politics  can fix what's wrong with America we're  having asked a libertarian day to here  here in Reason HQ and the latest  question comes from Eric Schmidt via  Facebook  what is the libertarian view of health  care and what can be done to fight it  Nick yeah well I'd I guess it's a fight  the Obama health care reform there's no  question that Obama care gets virtually  a hundred percent thumbs down from  libertarians primarily for a cut you  know for two basic reasons one is that  it includes a mandate which is troubling  from all sorts of perspectives and is  gonna be fought out in the Supreme Court  that clearly is gonna be the problem but  then there's a much larger question  because even if you could get everybody  to opt into the system the way that it's  been told there is no pricing mechanism  really in that system and this is the  problem again and again with the health  care system both in the so-called  private sector as well as in the public  sector whether it's Medicare or Medicaid  our health care system is believed to  somehow organize itself in ways that are  not at all like every other sector of  the economy which is that people buy and  sell stuff based on their perceptions of  what they want and the value worth it  price signals are completely absent from  the health care system are virtually  completely absent always and only  because of government regulations and  that is the problem so the problem with  the health care reform is that there are  no market signals in it and that means  it's never going to work very well what  can be done to fight it is to publicize  that and put out alternatives recentiy V  Reason magazine other free-market think  tanks have put out volume voluminous  material that shows how you can take the  same things that work in food delivery  or in selling widgets will work wonders  in health care to get more better health  care to more and more people
 

